   <h2>The verbs</h2>
   <p>Six verbs make the model. A handful of setup lines control the stage. A line starting with <code>#</code> or <code>//</code> is a comment, as is anything after a <code>#</code> that follows whitespace. Lines starting with <code>```</code> are ignored, so you can paste a markdown code block straight in.</p>
 
-  <div class="verb"><div class="head"><span class="name">mark</span><span class="what">a thing and its properties</span></div>
+  <div class="verb"><div class="head"><span class="name">mark</span><span class="what">put a thing on the stage; the same id again updates it in place</span></div>
   <div class="sig">mark &lt;id&gt; [kind] [category] key=value …</div>
   <div class="body">
     <p>Declares a thing. <code>kind</code> is one of <a href="#kinds">the eight mark kinds</a>; leave it out and the schema picks one. A bare word that isn't a kind is the <b>category</b> (one per mark). Everything else is <code>key=value</code>.</p>
